ot is a congenital condition diagnosed at birth or in utero). The Ponseti method is used in infants, not 18-year-olds. The examination section is severely corrupted with massive repetitive placeholder text ('*15 degrees (normal 10-15 degrees)' repeated ~28 times), indicating a generation failure. There is no treatment plan, no differential diagnosis, no special tests, no functional goals, no red flag screening, and no physiothera", "clinical_msk_score": 0.1923, "judge_tag": "compact:claude-sonnet-4-6"}
{"model_pair": "medgemma3", "name": "A0_tuned_teacher", "seed": 0, "case_id": 164, "title": "Clubfoot", "sample_idx": 0, "generation": "Case Study: Clubfoot\n\nClubfoot (Congenital Talipes Equinovarus) is a birth defect that affects the foot, causing it to turn inward and downward, resembling the shape of a club. It is the most common congenital foot deformity. The deformity is characterized by a fixed equinus (plantarflexion), varus (inversion), adduction, and cavus (high arch) of the foot. The calf muscle is usually short and tight. The child usually presents with a flatfoot and the foot is held in equinus.\n\nThe condition is often bilateral. The foot is usually rigid and the child may have difficulty walking.\n\nThe deformity is typically present at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe deformity is usually not noticeable at birth.\n\nThe def