{"model_pair": "medgemma3", "name": "C_ted_lite", "seed": 2, "case_id": 145, "title": "Clubfoot", "sample_idx": 0, "generation": "Case Study: Clubfoot\n\nAbstract\n\nThe case of a patient with Clubfoot is presented to illustrate how the management of the condition can be implemented and successful.\n\nKey words\n\nClubfoot\n\nClient characteristics\n\nA 45-year-old male with a history of hypertension and diabetes, who has developed Clubfoot due to a recent injury and subsequent foot deformity.\n\nPatient History\n\nThe patient is a 45-year-old male with a history of hypertension and diabetes, who has developed Clubfoot due to a recent injury and subsequent foot deformity. The patient has also had a past history of right lower extremity joint disease.\n\nMedical History\n\nThe patient was diagnosed with Clubfoot due to a recent injury and subsequent foot deformity. He has also been prescribed a blood pressure medication for hypertension. He has also had a history of diabetes, which has reduced his blood sugar levels. He has also been prescribed a diabetes medication for his blood sugar levels.\n\nExamination Findings\n\nThe patient has developed Clubfoot due to a recent injury. The patient has been prescribed a blood pressure medication for hypertension. He has also been prescribed a blood sugar medication for his blood sugar levels.\n\nIn addition to the patient's physical history, he has been prescribed a blood pressure medication for hypertension. He has also been prescribed a blood sugar medication for his blood sugar levels.\n\nClinical Findings\n\nThe patient has developed Clubfoot due to a recent injury and subsequent foot deformity. The patient has also been prescribed a blood pressure medication for hypertension. He has also been prescribed a blood sugar medication for his blood sugar levels.\n\nThe patient has developed Clubfoot due to a recent injury and subsequent foot deformity. The patient has also been prescribed a blood pressure medication for hyperte